# Planner per-rect LOW routability on a multi-rect block's notch
# (teg_multirect_status.md open 3).
#
# Geometry: L is a multi-rect `thru` block — tall arm (0,0)-(100,400) +
# base (0,0)-(400,100); the notch x=100-400, y=100-400 is OPEN ground, and
# cut CAPACITY is carved per rect (low_layer_keepouts), so LOW routing in
# the notch is physically fine.  A and B sit INSIDE the notch (and inside
# L's union bbox), and the d[4] bus between them is a short vertical hop a
# LOW layer should carry: M5's span_min 300 penalizes the 50-unit stub on
# TOP, so the honest choice is M3.
#
# Before the per-rect fix, `low_seg_obstructed` judged the UNION bbox: both
# segment endpoints lay "inside the cell" (the union), the whole hop was
# priced 9999 on every LOW layer, and the planner escalated it to TOP (M5)
# — the split-brain this flow pins (capacity said routable, the obstruction
# predicate said crossing).  After the fix the hop routes on M3.
# test_planner_notch_low.py asserts the M3 assignment and clean audits.

def_layer 2 M2 H 50
def_layer 3 M3 V 50
def_layer 4 M4 H TOP 50 span_min 300
def_layer 5 M5 V TOP 50 span_min 300

def_track_pattern 2 0 VDD 2 1 _ 1 1 _ 1 1 _ 1 1 _ 1 1
def_track_pattern 3 0 VDD 2 1 _ 1 1 _ 1 1 _ 1 1 _ 1 1
def_track_pattern 4 0 VDD 2 1 _ 1 1 _ 1 1 _ 1 1 _ 1 1
def_track_pattern 5 0 VDD 2 1 _ 1 1 _ 1 1 _ 1 1 _ 1 1

add_block L rect 0 0 100 400 rect 0 0 400 100
add_block A 150 150 250 250
add_block B 150 300 250 400

add_bus d[4] A.o B.i

run_bundler STRICT
generate_topologies
# Make the span-mismatch term decisive: the 50-unit hop pays 2.5 on TOP
# (span_min 300, kSpan 0.01) vs base_cost_non_top's span-scaled ~0.5 on LOW,
# so an unobstructed M3 wins and an obstructed one (the union-bbox bug)
# escalates to M5.
set_planner_param kSpan 0.01
run_planner
run_nuts
check_design nuts
run_detailed_nuts
check_design dnuts
report_wl
